Ambiguity Intolerance:
The diplomatic juxtaposition (Trump’s “progress in talks” versus ongoing Hormuz casualties) exemplifies a classic ambiguity challenge. However, node processing separates these into parallel but unrelated streams, avoiding the cognitive load of holding conflicting claims simultaneously. The result is a low-ambiguity-perceived environment despite objective ambiguity. Status remains elevated; trend nudged to +2.5% (from +2.4%).

