Multiple items offer irony-rich material: World Cup hydration breaks in Qatari summer, red cards and VAR as bureaucratic transparency theatre, a five-year parole denial for an NFL player alongside a year-old air crash where justice remains elusive, and a ceasefire “progress” that excludes dead sailors. These are almost certainly processed literally by the vast majority of nodes. The disconnect is institutional rather than individual—the Linguistic Infrastructure’s narrative formatting strips ironic valence. Status warning, trend increased to +5.6% (from +5.4%).

